kind of topic I like seeing discussed now and then.)

Here is *my interpretation* of what I meant (there's infinite 
recursion here):

The extropian philosophy of More et al, and sometimes this list,
is/was lacking in humanistic topics- things that have relevance to our
day-to-day lives. Yes, the philosophy, cryptography, anarchy, PPL, etc
are important, but our lives are usually spent with things like: eating,
sleeping, talking with our loved ones, programming on the computer, 
reading, excercising , talking with our neighbor, solving problems, 
etc etc. So how can we apply extropian ideas to these more every-day, 
humanistic things?  I listed some suggestions of things to look into
and I discuss how you might get more female and lurker participation if
these topics are discussed more often.

Since I'm a different person than I was when I wrote that long essay, 
this is my *current* interpretation of what I wrote.  And I must say the
response was fantastic, and I've loved all of the topics that have come
out of it.

So I think that Betsy and Romana each got my interpretation partially right.

